-990-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The questions made the leap into real life because we adapted them to the exchange, not because we followed the sheet unchanged."],"options":["The visitor exchange shows that the prepared sequence needed no adaptation.","The unexpected story showed that our prepared questions could not contribute anything.","The questions made the leap into real life because we adapted them to the exchange, not because we followed the sheet unchanged."]},"advanced-native-990-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The pause technique made the leap into real life when I used it to let visitors ask questions during the tour. I stopped filling every gap with more explanation.","A skill from drama class could make the leap into real life by changing how I guide visitors. Leaving time for questions makes the tour a conversation rather than a continuous speech."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-991', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-991-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Questions grounded in a resident’s actual access experience."],"options":["Another copy of the chapter with the same questions.","A decision to avoid talking to residents about the route.","Questions grounded in a resident’s actual access experience.","Proof that none of the chapter’s information was accurate."]},"advanced-native-991-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["We had been living inside textbooks and needed to connect the account with direct experience.","The resident could help us notice practical questions beyond the sample.","We wanted observations from the route to inform our discussion of change.","The chapter did not show all the access issues people encountered."],"options":["We had been living inside textbooks and needed to connect the account with direct experience.","The resident could help us notice practical questions beyond the sample.","We wanted observations from the route to inform our discussion of change.","The chapter did not show all the access issues people encountered."]},"advanced-native-991-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["I do not want to keep living inside textbooks; comparing actual plants will show where I need more practice."],"options":["The manual alone gives me enough evidence to label uncertain plants without comparing their features on site.","The walk requires us to stop using reference material for uncertain features.","I do not want to keep living inside textbooks; comparing actual plants will show where I need more practice."]},"advanced-native-991-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Textbooks should never be consulted again."],"options":["Study limited to texts may miss direct experience.","Textbooks should never be consulted again.","Reading can be connected with observation or use."]},"advanced-native-991-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We need not keep living inside textbooks, but we can use the chapter as background while checking it against observations."],"options":["The walk makes the useful background irrelevant, so we should omit it.","We should ignore the resident’s access questions because they are absent from the sample.","We need not keep living inside textbooks, but we can use the chapter as background while checking it against observations."]},"advanced-native-991-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["I do not want to keep living inside textbooks, so I will turn the consent principles into a clear invitation. My neighbour should know that questions can be declined and permission withdrawn later.","Instead of living inside textbooks and reciting definitions, I will practise explaining the choices my neighbour has before agreeing to the interview."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
